10 stories: Redrawing the ministries before naming the ministers: Hichilema asks Parliament to approve the creation, merger and dissolution of ministries, with Nalumango to move the motion (lead); Censure him, do not defend him: Simutanyi tells the UPND to hold the President to account over a Cabinet of four, as party officials say the Constitution sets no deadline; K52.6 million of inputs to inactive and double-dipping farmers: an agriculture foundation demands a FISP investigation after the Auditor-General's findings; A K2.2 billion test of appetite the day before the budget: Access Bank says Thursday's Treasury bill auction will show what investors think of the government's borrowing; 4,509,005 children to reach in a week: Chilengi launches Child Health Week and says the services should be routine, not an annual campaign; Past 1,300 cases and 27 deaths: the cholera outbreak has reached 18 districts in six provinces, with Lusaka carrying more than half the count and Chibombo most of the rest; 'The State is not ready to prosecute': Mundubile, Zulu and 16 others argue that investigating after charge cannot justify holding them, a day before their bail hearing resumes; 'Don't look down on yourselves, girls': Kanyemba calls the U-17 World Cup bad for Zambia, apologises to the fans and says the Copper Princesses need far more games at this level; Five pieces that survived a flooded studio: Emmanuel Chisenga, 24, of Lusaka becomes the first Zambian to win an Absa L'Atelier Ambassador Award; Five presidents on the page and one missing: the Zambia Daily Mail issues an 'unreserved apology to the nation' for leaving the late Edgar Lungu out of its Independence supplement.

